{"ts":"2026-11-12T10:21:41.227Z","actor":"claude","stage":"factcheck","action":"factcheck.review","details":{"verdict":"pass","notes":"Semantic check: the radiant is a direction, not a source, and the script says exactly that ('the meteors do not come from there'). Parent body is asteroid 3200 Phaethon per the IMO fact, so 'asteroid, not a comet' is right; the mechanism fact covers 'Earth runs into the stream, grains burn up high in the atmosphere'. The parallel-path/perspective explanation is the NASA definition of the radiant, and the driving-into-snow analogy is a comparison, not a claim. Numbers: 73 deg at 01:52 on 14 Dec (radiant fact, its maximum at 50N) and 150/h is the ideal-sky ZHR, stated as such. The closing advice that radiant altitude matters as much as the exact peak is standard meteor-observing practice. Image is real Arecibo radar imagery of Phaethon, credited on screen."},"gitSha":"395ad8b"}
